# @PROJECT@ .gitignore
#
# Legal rule (inherited from n64lle): ROM bytes are NEVER committed.
roms/*
!roms/README.md

# ROM-DERIVED GENERATED CODE — gitignored PENDING THE POSTURE DECISION.
#
# n64lle docs/05-PROPOSAL.md §10 specifies per-game repos hold "committed
# generated/". docs/DISTRIBUTION-POSTURE.md is an explicit DRAFT recommending
# Posture A (patcher-only: nothing ROM-derived ever leaves project hosting) and
# reserves the call for the owner "before any public artifact ships". Those two
# disagree. Until the owner rules, generated/ stays local: the reversible
# choice. Flip these two lines (and only these) once the posture is decided.
generated/*
!generated/README.md

# THE USER'S FILES, never the repo's. settings.toml is written by the launcher
# and input.cfg by its Configure page; both are per-machine (absolute ROM paths,
# pad GUIDs, scancodes). game.toml — the committed declared contract — is the
# one config file that IS source, and nothing in this build writes it.
settings.toml
settings.toml.bad
input.cfg
keybinds.ini

# Build trees (any variant).
build*/
out/
cmake-build-*/

# Captured frames from tools/frame_probe.c — observation output, not source.
captures/

# CMake noise
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeUserPresets.json
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
Testing/
install_manifest.txt
compile_commands.json

# Ninja / Make
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log
build.ninja
rules.ninja
Makefile

# Compiled objects, libraries, executables
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb

# Editor / OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
